{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552314-cosmology-vs-spirit-lore-knowledges","id":1552314,"title":"Cosmology vs (Spirit) Lore Knowledges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-12T17:49:14-07:00","id":1552314,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Cosmology vs (Spirit) Lore Knowledges","content":"If a player takes Cosmology 4, would you require them to also take Spirit Lore if they wanted to be a Summoner? <br /> <br /> My thought is the game has so much secondary skill bloat, I'd stick with Cosmology 4 with a specailty in (Umbrood Courts) or similar as enough. However, others may think differently, so thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T18:30:40-07:00","id":1552316,"title":"","content":"I'm no a fan of Ability bloat, so I'd be fine leaving everything under Occult.<br /> <br /> That said, IMO, Cosmology is more concerned with the &quot;geography&quot; of the Umbra, and Spirit Lore (or Lores for some people's preferences) is more concerned with the &quot;biology&quot; of the Umbra. Cosmology is about knowing the dominant Reality of different Umbral Realms, how to navigate the Umbra as you get farther from Earth/material plane, and so on. Spirit Lore is more about identifying the kind of spirit, what sort of chiminage would be appropriate, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T18:39:43-07:00","id":1552318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552314-cosmology-vs-spirit-lore-knowledges?p=1552316#post1552316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm no a fan of Ability bloat, so I'd be fine leaving everything under Occult.<br /> <br /> That said, IMO, Cosmology is more concerned with the &quot;geography&quot; of the Umbra, and Spirit Lore (or Lores for some people's preferences) is more concerned with the &quot;biology&quot; of the Umbra. Cosmology is about knowing the dominant Reality of different Umbral Realms, how to navigate the Umbra as you get farther from Earth/material plane, and so on. Spirit Lore is more about identifying the kind of spirit, what sort of chiminage would be appropriate, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit Lore (who to talk to and how) Cosmology (were to find who and what you want). A good choice in an Umbra centered campaign. For a Campaign not centered in the Umbra, Heavy Arms is right. Use Occult for both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T18:55:02-07:00","id":1552319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552314-cosmology-vs-spirit-lore-knowledges?p=1552316#post1552316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm no a fan of Ability bloat, so I'd be fine leaving everything under Occult.<br /> <br /> That said, IMO, Cosmology is more concerned with the &quot;geography&quot; of the Umbra, and Spirit Lore (or Lores for some people's preferences) is more concerned with the &quot;biology&quot; of the Umbra. Cosmology is about knowing the dominant Reality of different Umbral Realms, how to navigate the Umbra as you get farther from Earth/material plane, and so on. Spirit Lore is more about identifying the kind of spirit, what sort of chiminage would be appropriate, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea even where to start with Occult in m20, I don't even use it. The game will be OoH focused with an interest in summoning, but not feasible until the PCs sort out how to safely summon through the avatar storm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T00:00:09-07:00","id":1552354,"title":"","content":"If summoning is the focus and everyone is OoH, then having both as distinct Abilities may be a good idea. Overall, narrow chronicle concepts are a good reason to revise some of the Abilities used. On the other hand, you'll probably want to cut out <b>Technology</b> and just use <b>Craft</b>.<br /> <br /> Other than that, my way of dealing with bloat is to let different Abilities solve the same rolls with a +/- 1 difficulty modifier, just so I can let the players feel free to take whatever they think is better for their characters. Otherwise I use whatever is in the character sheet simply because it's easier.<br /> <br /> But as others said, Lore and Cosmology in this case cover distinct aspects of the Umbra. In a typical game it would be ok to let them both do the same things, but the concepts don't overlap as much as it seems (it's distinct enough for Geography and Anthropology to be completely distinct sciences).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}